formation and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " How Much or How Many?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use quantifiers to express quantities and amounts. There are various quantifiers you can use to express a small amount or a large amount."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.  You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br />  less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any /not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of/lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> 0, nothing<br /> to ask about / say there is not<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Measurements (Nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pound<br />pint<br />  quart<br />   dozen<br /> slice<br />  case\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than half a kilogram at 454 g<br /> a little less than half a liter<br /> a little less than one liter<br /> 12 pieces<br /> a cut piece from a whole<br /> a paper case of 6, 12 or 24 bottles\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Vanessa needs to cook a pound of chicken for the meal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sally brought a quart of ice cream. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Peter brought a half dozen pieces of naan."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Is it necessary?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " \u201c<span class=\"strong\">Have got</span> to\u201d is used to express necessity. It is more commonly used in British English. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u201cHave got to\u201d has irregular forms in the past and future. Look at the chart below."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>I/You/We/They</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have got</span> to<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ve got</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>He/She</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has got</span> to<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">'s got</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had</span> to</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ will + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span> + to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have got to finish your homework tonight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to finish your homework last night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will have to finish your homework tonight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We've got to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We had to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We will have to arrive early to get seats.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You've got to wash your hands before you start cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to wash my hands before I started cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will have to wash your hands before you start cooking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You must serve the food as soon as it's ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I had to serve the food as soon as it was ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I will have to serve the food as soon as it is ready.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What have you got to do there?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What did you have to do there?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What will you have to do there?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cut a thin flat piece from a whole, like a loaf of bread, or ham."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter sliced the baby cucumbers before getting to Vanessa's place."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about food and cooking."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a measurement used in the U.S. and the U.K. equal to almost 500 ml "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter brought a pint of yogurt to help soften the spicy taste."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enge